    "long_instructions": "## Sound Designer\r\n\r\nMake the program play a different note each time it runs.\r\n\r\n1. Review the code and ask AI Tutor how `play_note()` works.\r\n2. Use `randint()` to store a random note in the variable. Notes can be from 48 to 84.\r\n3. Update the `play_note()` command to use your variable.\r\n4. Run the program several times and listen for what changes.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from theater import *\nfrom random import randint\n\n# Sound\nplay_note(60, 10)\n\n# Background\nset_fill_color(\"indigo\")\ndraw_rectangle(0, 0, 400, 400)\n\n# Decorative icons\nset_text_color(\"aqua\")\nset_text_height(34)\ndraw_text(\"♪\", 45, 80)\ndraw_text(\"♫\", 310, 95)\ndraw_text(\"♪\", 340, 250)\ndraw_text(\"♫\", 35, 285)\n\n# Cassette body\nset_fill_color(\"pink\")\ndraw_rectangle(70, 130, 260, 145)\n\n# Cassette label\nset_fill_color(\"ivory\")\ndraw_rectangle(95, 150, 210, 38)\n\n# Cassette reels\nset_fill_color(\"white\")\ndraw_ellipse(105, 190, 65, 65)\ndraw_ellipse(230, 190, 65, 65)\n\nset_fill_color(\"black\")\ndraw_ellipse(125, 210, 25, 25)\ndraw_ellipse(250, 210, 25, 25)\n\n# Tape window\nset_fill_color(\"gray\")\ndraw_rectangle(165, 210, 70, 20)\n\n# Bottom details\nset_fill_color(\"purple\")\ndraw_rectangle(105, 250, 190, 12)\n\nset_text_color(\"black\")\nset_text_height(20)\ndraw_text(\"MIX TAPE\", 150, 176)\n\nset_text_color(\"white\")\nset_text_height(26)\ndraw_text(\"Random Note\", 120, 330)\n\nplay()",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
